  "cil_liability": true,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed sub-division of the existing residential curtilage would result in the creation of a residential plot that due to its siting, size and relationship to neighbouring properties and the surrounding area would represent an incongruous form of development that would be detrimental to the pattern of development and character and appearance of the area. This would be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework 2026; Policies D3 and H2 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD6, DMD7, DMD8 and DMD37 of the Development Management Document (2014",
    "The proposed development fails to provide a clearly defined and convenient pedestrian means of access to the property resulting in a substandard form of accommodation for future occupiers and would unduly detract from the privacy of the existing occupiers of No. 27. The proposal is contrary to PolicyD3 and D6 of the London Plan, Policies CP30 of Core Strategy and DMD6, DMD8 and DMD 37 and DMD47 of the Development Management Document.",
    "In the absence of an up-to-date parking stress survey, the applicant has failed to demonstrate that on-street parking demand generated by the proposed dwelling, which would have no off-street parking, could be accommodated on the surrounding highway network without resulting in unacceptable parking stress, to the detriment of highway safety and the amenity of local residents. The proposal is therefore contrary to Policies T6 and T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DMD 8 and DMD 45 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ]
